    "effect": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Effect",
      "value": "You summon a colorful butterfly that flaps its wings once. This sets a chain of connected events in motion. You determine the general outcome of each event (“Snow is falling on Dragon Peak”), but not the details. The connection does not have to be obvious, as your magic works in mysterious ways. Each step in the chain takes up to a full day to resolve. After each event, roll a [[d20]]. If the roll is equal to the number of events caused by the spell, or lower, the spell ends. You cannot end the spell voluntarily — a high enough roll always causes the next event."
    },
